{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : T \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Sch_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nu : (\\Sch/T)_{syntomic} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/S)_{syntomic},\n\\quad\nV/T \\longmapsto V/S\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nv : (\\Sch/S)_{syntomic} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/T)_{syntomic},\n\\quad\n(U \\to S) \\longmapsto (U \\times_S T \\to T).\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_{big} :\n\\Sh((\\Sch/T)_{syntomic})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Sh((\\Sch/S)_{syntomic})\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f_{big}^{-1}(\\mathcal{G})(U/T) = \\mathcal{G}(U/S)$", "MATH_0008": "$f_{big, *}(\\mathcal{F})(U/S) = \\mathcal{F}(U \\times_S T/T)$", "MATH_0009": "$f_{big}^{-1}$", "MATH_0010": "$f_{big!}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-big-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c4996dc5df58227becdebdc0a40c0a278d67e8fb4683fe169b965aff43c7105e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:adfce18d0e7f0836a6cb64f32d5856840a65fa50e6b10e962b4e4270cd1c8532", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a big syntomic site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism in <MATH_0003>.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0004>\nis cocontinuous, and has a continuous right adjoint\n<MATH_0005>\nThey induce the same morphism of topoi\n<MATH_0006>\nWe have <MATH_0007>.\nWe have <MATH_0008>.\nAlso, <MATH_0009> has a left adjoint <MATH_0010> which commutes with\nfibre products and equalizers.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:47c5d62b6d4ea7a348de6f93289288109537cd41211c1d28ca0af0ade93da9cd", "unit_id": "tag:04HD:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u$", "MATH_0002": "$f_{big}^{-1}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_{big!}$", "MATH_0004": "$v$", "MATH_0005": "$U/T$", "MATH_0006": "$V/S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Mor_S(u(U), V) = \\Mor_T(U, V \\times_S T)$", "MATH_0008": "$f_{big, *}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-lemma-when-shriek}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-preserve-equalizers}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-lemma-have-functor-other-way}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-lemma-have-functor-other-way-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab3d0cb40f076f0591499f472d52f7ec6dfae663795aaa76df5076802ef3f249", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6784e37b38363f2c3747861317c4165d89a34c1b085c2fdc10140d85c8caada", "source_text": "The functor <MATH_0001> is cocontinuous, continuous, and commutes with fibre products\nand equalizers. Hence\nSites, Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>\napply and we deduce the formula\nfor <MATH_0002> and the existence of <MATH_0003>. Moreover,\nthe functor <MATH_0004> is a right adjoint because given <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006>\nwe have <MATH_0007>\nas desired. Thus we may apply\nSites, Lemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004> to get the\nformula for <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2a663295e642bc4f32ac4f07a2363bd80c7593def177190efa7101baf2afacf5", "unit_id": "tag:04HD:proof"}
